{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Investigation narration (moved out of the description for plan-review admission)\n\nThe first plan review (`reviewed_at 1789495982193956893`, verdict BLOCK) fired a single blocking\nfinding, P4 `oversize`: the description was 8218 chars against the 8000-char admission cap. Per\nthe remediation guidance, the narration below was moved here and the description tightened to\n6118 chars; no work was split.\n\n### How the root cause was established\n\n1. Located the three candidate configs: `~/.copilot/mcp-config.json` (user-level, held `serena`\n   plus `atlassian`), `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.mcp.json` (project-level, held only `rebar`),\n   and the untracked `.agents/mcp_config.json` (Claude's own serena config).\n2. Read `~/.copilot/logs/process-1789493292635-48702.log`, which carried the verbatim cause —\n   `uvx` rebuilding `serena-agent` from git and `git init` exiting 128 on `~/.gitconfig`. The\n   broken pipe on `initialize` is a downstream symptom, not the fault.\n3. Confirmed `~/.copilot/settings.json` sets `sandbox.sandboxMcpServers: true` and that its\n   `sandbox.userPolicy.filesystem.readwritePaths` already lists `~/.local/share`, `~/.cache`,\n   `~/.serena`, and `~/.rebar-serena-mirror` — but not `~/.gitconfig`. That asymmetry is exactly\n   why a prebuilt binary works while a git build does not, and why no policy edit is needed.\n\n### Alternatives considered and rejected\n\n- **Whitelist `~/.gitconfig` in the sandbox policy.** Rejected: it widens a host-wide security\n  policy to work around a launcher that should not be touching git at all, and it leaves startup\n  dependent on upstream HEAD, so the server can still break when the ref moves.\n- **Pin `uvx --from git+...@<sha>`.** Rejected: still runs `git init` inside the sandbox on\n  every launch, so it does not fix the failure at all.\n- **Leave the entry user-scoped and only change the command.** Rejected: it fixes the crash but\n  keeps serena loading in every directory on the host and invisible to the repo, which is the\n  second of the two defects and the one `docs/mcp-client-setup.md:84-88` already has a\n  precedent against.\n\n### `${HOME}` expansion probe\n\nBefore committing a `${HOME}`-bearing path to a tracked file, the expansion was proven rather\nthan assumed. A scratch project at `/Users/joeoakhart/scratch/mcp-probe` declared a wrapper\nscript as its `command` and logged its own fully expanded argv; a headless `copilot -p` run\nagainst it showed both `command` and `args` expanded. The probe directory has since been\ndeleted.\n\n### Verification already performed on the live host\n\n- `uv tool install --from git+https://github.com/oraios/serena serena-agent` resolved\n  serena-agent 1.7.1.dev0 to `~/.local/share/uv/tools/serena-agent/bin/serena`.\n- The binary was smoke-tested directly over stdio JSON-RPC: `initialize` succeeded, 22 tools\n  were advertised, startup took roughly 2s, and no git subprocess ran.\n- After adding the project entry and running `copilot mcp remove serena` (backup written to\n  `~/.copilot/mcp-config.json.bak-<timestamp>`), a headless `copilot -p` run in this checkout\n  reported 22 serena tools, the latest log contained zero `MCP server connection failed` lines,\n  and `server_info` carried `name: \"Serena\"`. `copilot mcp list` shows serena only under\n  `Workspace servers`, and not at all from `$HOME`.\n\n### Incidental finding, not part of this ticket\n\nThe local `main` checkout carries an unlanded commit `7b92d821718` (\"Default make worktree to\n~/worktrees/rebar/<branch>\") that breaks `make worktree`: it places `@#` comment lines inside a\nshell line-continuation, so the shell parses `<branch>` as a redirect and the target dies with\n`/bin/sh: branch: No such file or directory`. `origin/main` (5c2d3e664fa) is unaffected. The\nworktree for this change was therefore created manually from `origin/main`. Raised here for\nvisibility; it needs its own ticket if the commit is intended to land."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789496423448699096,"uuid":"d6f80532-6d42-4e4d-a40b-6edce5d976c4"}